# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rift — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and must stay that
# way; nothing in this file should ever hold a real value.
#
# Every service below is documented in docs/integrations.md — what it is for,
# what it costs, and what happens when it is missing. Every public page renders
# with NONE of these set, and says what is not connected.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────── auth, database, files
# Project → Settings → API. The anon key is public by design; RLS is what
# protects the data, so never ship a table without a policy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# The same URL, without the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, for server-side code.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are inlined into the bundle at BUILD time, so a server
# reading one is pinned to whatever was set when it was compiled — changing the
# runtime environment does nothing, and the process keeps talking to the old
# project while every variable on the machine says otherwise. Set both; they
# should hold the same value.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Server-only. Bypasses RLS entirely — never expose it to the browser and never
# prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Needed for migrations, seeding, and jobs.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Server-only. Signs the short-lived tokens the public forms hand back: the
# Equb form's second step, an offer's upload, and the offer upload's pass.
# Falls back to the service key when unset; set its own so rotating one does
# not void the other. With neither, the offer upload asks for no pass.
# RIFT_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Set to `local` to run auth against localStorage with no Supabase project at
# all. Useful offline; remove it for anything real.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_MODE=local


# ── Sentry ────────────────────────────────────────── errors and performance
# Failures must surface, never fail silently (docs/handoff.md §5 rule 4).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# Optional server/edge override; falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN.
# SENTRY_DSN=

# Source-map upload on `next build`. Set in CI and on Vercel, not locally —
# without a token, `next.config.ts` disables sourcemap upload rather than failing.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=


# ── Brevo ──────────────────────────────────── transactional email (and the lead text)
# Missing key = every send no-ops cleanly and reports `skipped`. That is the
# correct dev behaviour and it is deliberate: see lib/db/email.ts.
# If the API returns 401 "unrecognised IP", whitelist at Security → Authorised IPs.
# BREVO_API_KEY=
#
# The sending address, which Brevo must have verified. Without it every send is
# rejected at the API, so it is treated as missing configuration rather than
# defaulted — an unconfigured deployment reports "not configured" instead of
# failing every message with a confusing 400.
# BREVO_FROM_EMAIL=
# The sender name for the new-lead text to the agent's own phone (D40): up to 11
# letters, with SMS credits on the Brevo account and a phone number in Operations,
# Settings. Unset: lead alerts go by email only, and /api/health (with the cron
# secret) says so.
# BREVO_SMS_SENDER=


# ── Site ──────────────────────────────────────── where this deployment lives
# The public origin, used by the sitemap, robots.txt, the canonical links and
# every social share card. OPTIONAL: when it is unset the origin is derived
# from Vercel's own VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL, so the common case needs no
# configuration. Set it when there is a custom domain — a sitemap and a share
# card naming a vercel.app URL for a site that has a real domain split the
# product's search authority in two.
#
# It used to be required and nobody had set it, so /sitemap.xml served a
# valid document with zero URLs and robots.txt omitted its Sitemap: line, for
# the whole life of the deployment, returning 200 throughout. See
# lib/core/site.ts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com


# ── Scheduler ────────────────────────── the nurture cadence and the sweep
# Shared secret for /api/nurture/run and /api/retention/sweep. Without it both
# endpoints refuse to run at all — an unauthenticated endpoint that sends email
# on demand is a way to have your sending reputation destroyed by a stranger
# with curl, and one that deletes rows needs no explanation.
#
# On Vercel, set this and the platform attaches it to the cron invocation
# automatically. Check it is working with `checks.retention` on /api/health,
# not with `checks.scheduler` — the second only says the secret exists, which
# is what let both jobs sit broken and green for the life of the deployment.
# CRON_SECRET=


# ── Calendar ───────────────────────────────────────── consultation booking
# Speed-to-lead is only real once a stranger can take a slot without a human in
# the path.
# Without both of these the booking screen asks for a rough preference instead
# of offering times. It never invents plausible slots: a person who picks
# 6pm Thursday and finds it never existed has been told a lie at the exact
# moment they decided to trust the product.
# CAL_API_KEY=
# CAL_EVENT_TYPE_ID=
#
# The agent's timezone, used to label slots and to book in. Defaults to
# America/New_York.
# RIFT_TIMEZONE=America/New_York


# ── Not yet chosen ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are needed by features already specified. Until they exist, the code paths must degrade honestly rather than pretend — see
# docs/integrations.md for exactly how.
#
# SMS to leads. Without it, every text step in the nurture cadence permanently
# downgrades to email (lib/core/nurture.ts, resolveChannel). The TCPA consent
# gate is already built and is what makes texting lawful at all. (The new-lead
# text to the agent's own phone is BREVO_SMS_SENDER, above.)
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=
#
# E-signature. Representation agreements gate the client journey and block
# plan publishing (lib/core/seam.ts, canPublish). Today `rep` is a status
# field with nothing behind it.
# ESIGN_API_KEY=
